 trustworthy scoreboard, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sase instructions show`, and a handoff-aware readout prove the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]result and support the soak.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]e3_explicit_delivery_cutover.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/e3_explicit_delivery_cutover.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1ko[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1ko/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Provider channel and suppression spikes, with outcomes [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]recorded on the epic[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]spikes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]spikes: run cheap direct CLI probes for Claude native exclusion, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]auto-memory, and the system-prompt files; Codex project-doc suppression,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fresh shadow state, and fork children; Muse without workspace trust; and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Grok memory v2. Record each outcome and CLI version as a structured note[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on the epic bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Instruction manifest wire v2 in sase-core (delivery slots and [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fallback), binding, adapter, pin move[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]delivery-wire[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]delivery-wire: bump the instruction manifest wire to v2. Add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]subagent delivery slot, the delivery fallback block, and the channel and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]slot invariants. Keep v1 manifests readable. Update the binding, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Python adapter constants, the golden fixtures in both repos, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core pin.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scoreboard sees dismissed agents, and the new sase [/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]instructions show command[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]run-discovery[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]run-discovery: make verify and render enumerate and resolve hidden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](dismissed) agents. Fail loudly when an agent name resolves to nothing. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Teach the manifest reader about helper manifests, and fix the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-purpose coverage denominator. Add `sase instructions show NAME`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]which prints an agent's recorded bundle and manifest and checks the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stored bytes against the manifest digest.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Handoff-aware declaration and memory-read readout, with the [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]pre-cutover baseline attached[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]readout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after run-discovery[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]readout: add `sase instructions readout`. Per provider and delivery [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mode, it classifies finished root runs as accepted, plan handoff, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor handoff, not required, or miss, and joins memory reads per run. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Reproduce the planning-time baseline, and attach the pre-cutover [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline JSON to the epic.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Delivery-plan hook, active delivery, atomic legacy fallback, [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]and helper manifests at the boundary[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]delivery-plan[dim] · [dim][/dim]after delivery-wire[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]delivery-plan: add the `llm_instruction_delivery` hookspec and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]DeliveryPlan model, with declared-legacy built-ins. The boundary [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolves the plan, renders the root bundle and (when declared) the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]helper bundle, validates transport, writes v2 manifests, and exposes the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]active delivery to adapters. It records session ids and falls back [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]atomically to legacy delivery with a deduplicated notification. Bundle [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]files become 0644.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Channel-aware, occurrence-exact scoreboard counting and the [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]conformance check[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]channel-counting[dim] · [dim][/dim]after run-discovery, delivery-plan[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]channel-counting: count layers across native and explicit channels by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]occurrence, not containment. Use what partial transcripts show. Add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bundle-marker column and helper marker checks, and associate sessions by[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marker and session id. Fix the Claude auto-memory and Muse [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]double-attribution misreads. Add the `instructions.conformance` doctor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Claude root bundle via system-prompt file, helper bundle, [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]exact-path native exclusion[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]claude[dim] · [dim][/dim]after spikes, delivery-plan, channel-counting[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]claude: create the `claude_explicit_instructions` sunset flag. When it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]is on, deliver the root bundle with `--append-system-prompt-file` and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the helper bundle with `--append-subagent-system-prompt-file`. Exclude [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE-owned root and home instruction files by exact path, and turn [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]auto-memory off per decision. Flag off restores E1's after-state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exactly.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Codex developer-instructions delivery, project-doc [/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]suppression, and shadow-home hygiene (folds sase-11s)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]codex[dim] · [dim][/dim]after spikes, delivery-plan, channel-counting[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]codex: create the `codex_explicit_instructions` sunset flag. When it is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on, deliver the whole root bundle through `developer_instructions`, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`project_doc_max_bytes=0` in SASE-managed projects only, and leave the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shadow home without any SASE AGENTS.md. Rebuild the shadow home from an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]allowlist so shared sqlite state is never linked (closes sase-11s), and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declare the subagent slot inherits_root.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Grok full-bundle rules and Muse prompt-prefix delivery[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]grok-muse[dim] · [dim][/dim]after spikes, delivery-plan, channel-counting[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]grok-muse: create the `grok_explicit_instructions` sunset flag, plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`muse_explicit_instructions` if the Muse spike passed. Grok's `--rules` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]carries the full root bundle, and memory v2 is set per decision. Muse [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gets the bundle as its prompt prefix without `--trust-workspace`, or is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declared legacy with no flag. Interrupt and wait reconstruction never [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nests a second bundle.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live acceptance probes, decision record, docs, and acceptance[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]record[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]record[dim] · [dim][/dim]after readout, claude, codex, grok-muse[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]record: prove every exit criterion with harness probes in both flag [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]states (plus launch probes once the installed code has E3), the Claude [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]helper probe, readout JSON, and parity in all four projects. Write the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decision record, the docs, and the inventory update. Attach the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance record, with its notes for E4, to the epic.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1ko","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1ko.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-d3efb45dd5449a20e0c48c9d5b95fe11","started_at":"2026-10-13T22:11:36.780684+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"214b7baa8261623307a118f850926c1454c6d1c42caa1f7677438addd8a059d8","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.sase-1ko.9/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"df04d4ef9e6ffc388cbde6fa7548c8aa2981922e76eb047cda955783938c225e","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.sase-1ko.9/meta.json","size_bytes":700},"prompt":{"digest":"91db5b31fad87432c2d6fa0143294fc37749af38bafb42b91967dced8b9fd152","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.sase-1ko.9/promp